  "description": "<p>There are broken links in the fedora documentation on the wiki:</p>\n\n<p> </p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://wiki.lyrasis.org/display/FEDORA51/Configuring+a+JMS+Event+Filter\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://wiki.lyrasis.org/display/FEDORA51/Configuring+a+JMS+Event+Filter</a> links to:</p>\n<ul>\n\t<li><a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/blob/master/fcrepo-webapp/src/main/resources/spring/eventing.xml\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/blob/master/fcrepo-webapp/src/main/resources/spring/eventing.xml</a></li>\n\t<li><a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/blob/master/fcrepo-webapp/src/main/resources/spring/fcrepo-config.xml#L176\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/blob/master/fcrepo-webapp/src/main/resources/spring/fcrepo-config.xml#L176</a></li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<p>These are the two I discovered, there might be more.</p>\n\n<p> </p>\n\n<p>By looking at the links I assume the cause is switching the branch from master to main.</p>",
